            "id": "4946369",
            "title": "BITB: Diversifying Risk With Bitcoin",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\"><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"The hand palm holds stylized gold bitcoin coins in the air\" data-id=\"1785109925\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1040\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1785109925/image_1785109925.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">Valeriia Mitriakova/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>The Bitwise Bitcoin ETF (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/BITB\" title=\"Bitwise Bitcoin ETF\">BITB</a></span>) is a passively managed exchange-traded fund designed to track the performance of bitcoin. With the emergence of bitcoin spot ETFs in 2024, BITB is one of the many ETFs on the market for investors to choose from for allocation within a standard brokerage account. While bitcoin has historically been viewed as a speculative asset, many advisors have allocated client funds to the alternative asset in order to gain long-term exposure to the potential price appreciation of bitcoin. Given the volatile and speculative nature of trading bitcoin, investors should use precautions and fully understand the risks with respect to their investment horizon.</p> <h2>Why is Bitcoin a Speculative Trading Asset?</h2> <p>Bitcoin has undergone a number of cycles as a trading asset, initially considered a hedge against the broader equity markets. As bitcoin became more institutionalized, the trading patterns of bitcoin have become more correlated with the S&amp;P 500 Index (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/SPX\" title=\"S&amp;P 500 Futures\">SPX</a>) up until October 2025. Following the <a href=\"https://www.fticonsulting.com/insights/articles/crypto-crash-october-2025-leverage-met-liquidity\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">major liquidation crisis</a> in October 2025, bitcoin entered into an inverse trading pattern with respect to the S&amp;P 500, diverging from the prior trading pattern associated with the Index.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"985\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1813\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"TradingView\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"348\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399696247487_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>TradingView</span></p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>Bitcoin holds no fundamental value beyond the price of the token, meaning that bitcoin’s intrinsic value cannot be estimated based on any factors other than supply and demand. Given this notion, bitcoin should be viewed as a speculative trading asset.</p> <p>Given the market depth, bitcoin has a tendency to trade in accordance with Elliott Wave Theory, providing some predictability during normal market conditions. Elliott Wave Theory should not be perceived as the Rule, meaning that the bitcoin’s trading pattern may not follow technical trading rules.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"985\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1814\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"TradingView\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"348\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399697037873_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>TradingView</span></p></figcaption></figure></p> <h3> </h3> <p>The price of bitcoin may be influenced by a number of exogenous factors, including public policy, inflation, interest rate policy, international trade, and global conflict, amongst others. In mid-2025, the <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/07/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-signs-genius-act-into-law/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">GENIUS Act</a> was signed into law as a regulatory framework for digital payments, creating more certainty in the stablecoin market. While this provided more guardrails for protecting users of the cryptocurrencies, the legislation had a limited impact on the price of bitcoin.</p> <p>Bitcoin is also expected to provide stability <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1059056025006756\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">during global conflict</a>, particularly during times of economic uncertainty and currency instability. This factor may no longer hold as the market likely views bitcoin as a standard risk asset rather than a currency hedge. This may mean that exogenous factors will have limited influence on the price of bitcoin, particularly during a technical trading cycle.</p> <h2>About Bitwise Bitcoin ETF</h2> <p>BITB was launched on January 10, 2024, by Bitwise with the Bank of New York Mellon as the Trust custodian on the NYSE Arca Exchange. The Trust’s digital asset custodian is Coinbase Custody Trust Company, where bitcoin is held across multiple wallets in cold storage as a security measure. Cold storage means that the bitcoin is held offline on hardware that has never been connected to the internet in a multi-layer storage vault.</p> <p>BITB currently has approximately $2.96 billion in net assets with an average of $49.7 million in share value changing hands on a daily basis, providing investors and traders with significant liquidity and market depth.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"232\" data-og-image-facebook=\"false\" data-og-image-google_news=\"false\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"false\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"false\" data-og-image-msn=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"false\" data-width=\"1197\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"Seeking Alpha\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"124\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/9/12/16009792-17892399694243886_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"><span>Seeking Alpha</span></p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>BITB tracks the performance of the CME CF Bitcoin Reference Rate – New York Variant. Given that BITB was designed to track the Index, BITB should not be expected to provide excess returns on investment.</p> <p>The core differentiators between bitcoin ETFs are fees and liquidity. For long-term investors, the ETF’s expense ratio may hold more weight for fund selection, whereas liquidity may be a critical quality for active traders. For the greatest market depth, the iShares Bitcoin Trust (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/IBIT\" title=\"iShares Bitcoin Trust ETF\">IBIT</a>) exhibits the greatest asset base and market depth. For the lowest fees, the Grayscale Bitcoin Mini Trust ETF (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/BTC\" title=\"Grayscale Bitcoin Mini Trust ETF\">BTC</a>) has an expense ratio of 15bps.</p> <h2>Investor Suitability</h2> <p>BITB can be deployed by both active and passive investors to gain exposure to the performance of bitcoin. Given the relatively low management fee and trading depth, BITB can be used as a component of a diversified portfolio strategy or for tactical positioning. From an asset allocation perspective, BITB will be considered as an alternative asset. Given the speculative nature, <a href=\"https://tokenist.com/blackrock-bitcoin-allocation-advisor-portfolios/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">advisors tend to allocate</a> 1-2% of the total portfolio weight to bitcoin ETFs in order to gain exposure while managing risk.</p> <h2>Risks Related to BITB</h2> <p>BITB provides indirect exposure to bitcoin, exposing investors to certain risks that should be considered prior to making a final investment decision. Bitcoin has a volatile nature and may substantially increase an investor’s risk profile. Bitcoin is considered as a speculative asset, meaning that the value of bitcoin cannot be measured against an economic weight. This means that the price of bitcoin is purely dictated based on the supply &amp; demand of the token. Before considering BITB or peer strategies, investors must evaluate their risk tolerance and how these ETFs may function within their broader portfolio strategies. Investors should also weigh liquidity, spread risk, and management fees when determining which ETF is most suitable for their investment needs.</p> <h2>Final Thoughts</h2> <p>BITB is a competitive bitcoin spot ETF in terms of liquidity and fees. Given the speculative nature of bitcoin, investors must weigh the risks associated with investing in the asset and whether it is suitable for their investment objectives. Given the volatile nature of bitcoin, these ETFs may be more suitable for investors with longer investment horizons.</p> <p>This article answers three questions about BITB:</p> <ol> <li>How does BITB track the performance of Bitcoin?</li> <li>What impacts how BITB performs?</li> <li>Which investors is BITC most suitable for?</li> </ol> <p><span><em>Editor's note:</em></span><em> This article is intended to provide a general overview of the ETF for educational purposes only and, unlike other articles on Seeking Alpha, does not offer an investment opinion about the ETF.</em></p></body></html>",
